_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 93
---
order: 93
---
short_label: X.93
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: If an area is contained by a rational straight line and a third apotome, then the side of the area is a second apotome of a medial straight line.
----
proof:

Let the area {AB} be contained by the rational straight line {AC} and the third apotome {AD}.

I say that the side of the area {AB} is a second apotome of a medial straight line.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="410" height="190" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="X.93 diagram" src="propX93.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // Joyce's figure: the area AB (ACBD) on the rational AC and the third
    // apotome AD, with the annex DG, E bisecting DG, F from the application
    // to AG, the parallels EH, FI, GK, the rectangles DFIB and IFGK, and the
    // squares LM (RMPL) and NO (PNQO) about the diameter PR, with SQ, TQ and
    // the gnomon arc UVW.
    // Added, all hidden at rest: solid twins FI, GK (initiallyHidden) so the
    // parallels stroke down from F and G; transparent segment targets
    // (;0;0;0); faceless twins ABh, LM, NO of the filled ACBD, RMPL, PNQO,
